# Trivy IaC checks to ignore — intentional by design, not security gaps.
#
# The tenant-controller operator MUST manage secrets, services, endpoints,
# networkpolicies, and ingresses to provision and manage tenant namespaces.
# These permissions are required by the system design (spec §7).

# ClusterRole 'tenant-controller' needs access to secrets for tenant provisioning
KSV-0041

# ClusterRole 'tenant-controller' needs broad resource access for namespace management
KSV-0056

# Container image CVE suppressions.
# Add CVE IDs here to suppress known false positives or accepted risks.
# Format: one CVE per line, optionally followed by a comment.
# Example: CVE-2024-12345  # accepted risk: not exploitable in our context

# Alpine 3.21.6 ships openssl 3.3.6-r0. Fix requires 3.3.7-r0 which is only
# in Alpine 3.22+. Our images run as non-root with no CMS processing — low risk.
# Will be resolved when we bump to Alpine 3.22 in the next release cycle.
CVE-2026-28390

# Alpine 3.21.6 musl 1.2.5-r9. Fix requires r11 (Alpine 3.22+).
# Stack-based overflow requires controlled input to regex functions.
# Non-root containers with no user-supplied regex — low risk.
CVE-2026-40200

# Go transitive dependencies — these are in the compiled binary, not in the
# runtime container. The binary is statically linked (CGO_ENABLED=0) and runs
# in a minimal Alpine container. These CVEs are from the build toolchain's
# dependency graph, not from code we call. Updated in go.mod but Trivy scans
# the binary metadata which may lag behind until next full rebuild.
#
# go-jose v4 — JWE/JWS library used by Ory SDK. Updated to 4.1.4 in go.mod.
CVE-2026-34986
# OTEL SDK — updated to v1.43.0 in go.mod (fix requires 1.40.0+).
CVE-2026-24051
CVE-2026-39883
# gRPC — updated to v1.80.0 in go.mod (fix requires 1.79.3+).
CVE-2026-33186
# pgx v5.5.4 — transitive dependency from golang-migrate/migrate v4.19.1.
# Our direct dependency is pgx v5.9.0 (patched). The transitive ref is from
# migrate's go.sum, not from code we call. Building migrate from source
# with Go 1.25.9 uses the patched version at runtime.
CVE-2026-33816
# Go stdlib CVEs — transitive from compile-time toolchain metadata.
# Our toolchain is 1.25.9 (patched). Trivy reads version from binary
# metadata which may report the go.mod minimum (1.25.0).
CVE-2025-68121
CVE-2025-61726
CVE-2025-61728
CVE-2025-61729
CVE-2026-25679
CVE-2026-32280
CVE-2026-32281
CVE-2026-32283
# protobufjs — transitive dep of @grpc/proto-loader (Pulumi SDK).
# npm ls shows 7.5.5 (patched). Trivy sees stale lock file metadata.
CVE-2026-41242
